# Output files and reports
*.log
*.txt
AD_Security_Audit_*.json
AD_Security_Audit_*.html
AD_Security_Audit_*.csv
AD_Privileged_Users_*.csv
ADSecurityAudit_Log_*.txt
AD_Security_Score_*.json

# Exception: curated reference samples for
# tools/New-ADSecurityAuditSyntheticFixtures.ps1 (see
# tools/synthetic-fixtures-samples/README.md) - intentionally checked in,
# unlike real audit output elsewhere in the repo, which the blanket
# patterns above exist to keep out. Without this exception, `git add`
# would silently ignore these files despite matching the patterns above
# exactly (same filename shape by design - they ARE the same file type,
# just synthetic).
!tools/synthetic-fixtures-samples/*.json
!tools/synthetic-fixtures-samples/*.html
!tools/synthetic-fixtures-samples/*.csv

# PowerShell transcripts
*_transcript.txt

# Temp files
*.tmp
*.temp
~$*

# IDE and editor files
.vscode/
.vs/
*.suo
*.user
*.sln.docstates

# OS generated files
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Secrets and credentials (should never be committed)
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
credentials.json
secrets.json
.env
